title HUNK55 — tap a filmstrip thumbnail, the cursor jumps there
prompt Take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first on the Season-A / double-seat road; approve my own design rounds and make progress before checking in; send each finished increment as its own signed round; STOP at the custody gates.
think Read the REMEMBER card's latest lap (HUNK54) and the two itinerary docs. The card names two in-assembly kg doors — a tap-to-jump on the filmstrip (HUNK50 cell index -> cursor position) and the screen scrolled (HUNK40-47) — and holds the session-that-travels crux for Keaton (the pond/apps<->brushstroke assembly-identity seam). Lindy-first crux-first: the tap-to-jump is the durable crux that makes HUNK54's read-only filmstrip navigable, staying entirely inside the brushstroke assembly (no held seam crossed, no gate reached).
think Read the pieces: edit_filmstrip.rye (HUNK54) tiles thumbnails and marks cursor.position; edit_touch_input.rye (HUNK50) classifies a pixel tap as x/cell_px; image/edit_cursor.rye (HUNK16) has undo/redo but no direct jump. A tap-to-jump is a multi-step navigation that must forget nothing (unlike push, which discards the redo tail) — so the cursor wants one additive primitive: seek(target), clamping to 0..=count.
think The crux to prove is HUNK52's no-drift discipline carried to the strip: the band a keeper TAPS equals the band the marker SHOWS. It falls out for free because paint is HUNK54's filmstrip unchanged (marker at cursor.position) and tap_at seeks cursor.position to the tapped band.
obs Added seek to image/edit_cursor.rye additively (clamps, forgets nothing; a no-op when target==position) with two invariants; proved it in HUNK16's own selftest (jump to 1, back to 3 byte-for-byte, clamp past count, seek to 0). The seek assert uses `or` (position==target or position==count) — a single logical claim, not the banned compound `and`.
obs Built brushstroke/edit_filmstrip_jump.rye FilmstripJump: owns one cursor + thumbnail geometry; band_px = tcols*cell_w (parallel of HUNK50's x/cell_px); tap_band classifies, tap_at seeks, paint delegates to HUNK54. Pure composition — no new render primitive, no new arithmetic beyond a clamped division, no new failure mode (a tap off the strip fires nothing, a zero thumbnail refuses BadThumb at open).
obs GREEN first metal run — the REDS #76 loom held (witness checks claims with native `assert out contains`, so the GREEN line's apostrophe-free phrasing is not even the risk it once was). HUNK54 filmstrip and HUNK16 cursor+seek GREEN beneath; tame_style_check bans clean; width-check exit 0; no compound asserts or bans in the two touched files.
